            "source_quote": "εἰ δὲ τὰ ἐναντία λέγων ἀποδείκνυσιν, τότε ἀληθεύει.",
            "english_quote": "But if he demonstrates the opposite, then he speaks truly.",
            "issue": "The conditional's general meaning is represented, but 'demonstrates the opposite' compresses λέγων and ἀποδείκνυσιν into one act. The Greek explicitly distinguishes saying the opposite from substantiating it, a relevant distinction in this argument about competing assertions.",
